<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sak Kʼukʼ</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 612–<a href="/years/615">615</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Muwaan Mat, Lady Sak Kʼukʼ, Lady Beastie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sak Kʼukʼ, also known as Muwaan Mat and Lady Beastie, was queen of the Maya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/city-state">city-state</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palenque">Palenque</a>. The daughter of Janahb <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kinich-janaab-pakal">Pakal</a>, who seems to have had no male heirs, she took the throne on 19 October 612, a few months after his death, and ruled until 615, when her son Kʼinich Janaab Pakal I succeeded her on reaching maturity. She seems to have kept considerable influence over Palenque in the early decades of his reign: Pakal's sarcophagus lid records her as the ruler who celebrated the sealing of the kʼatun in 633. She was probably also the mother of Ajen Yohl Mat, and she died in 640.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sak-k-uk.jpg" alt="Sak Kʼukʼ" width="190" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZacKukProfile.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palenque">Palenque</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/mexico">Mexico</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=17.48,-92.05&amp;year=613" aria-label="Palenque on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2050 1515 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Sak Kʼukʼ"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M2500 1785h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M2500 1785h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=17.48,-92.05&amp;year=613">What was here in 613 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
